                "href": "strava://segments/696322/leaderboard",
                "type": "overall",
                "name": "All-Time"
            }
        },
        "pacing_notes": "18th Street is one of the most consistent climbs in Pittsburgh, staying pretty consistently around 5-7%. The steepest gradients are found at the very start of the climb, averaging around 10% in between Mary and Mission Streets. There is a sneakily difficult section right after Corner Cafe where the gradients pick up slightly to ~8%. At this point, just think about making it to the mural you can see ahead of you - the climb levels off for a little bit as you make this turn, before slowly kicking up again to the light.",
        "summary": "18th is basically the easiest way to make it up Mt Washington that does not involve a car or funicular. Every other road, aside from Josephine, either has Dirty Dozen level gradients, or is heavily trafficked by cars.",
