        "total_elevation_gain": 90.2,
        "map": {
            "id": "s815373",
            "polyline": "spwuF~chgNTMHFDNA^GJC^[l@Kh@E^]~@GXKZANLb@ZRHHVv@X~BAj@Hb@DJPBPA`@KF?PJb@Nd@ZJJj@Jj@PDLEVKJ]D_A@a@DWHQLo@zAc@bBGp@CHSXEB"
        },
        "xoms": {
            "kom": "2:43",
            "qom": "3:37",
            "overall": "2:43",
            "destination": {
                "href": "strava://segments/815373/leaderboard",
                "type": "overall",
                "name": "All-Time"
            }
        },
        "pacing_notes": "Pacing Sycamore is fairly straightforward - just reach the hairpin about 2/3 of the way up the hill. Generally, the leadup to the hill involves a short period on Arlington, which is a short climb in its own. After the right onto Sycamore, you maintain a very consistent ~15% as you twist your way up the mountain. Making it to the hairpin is critical here as the climb quickly falls off here to a more pedestrian ~7% for a little bit. Make sure that you have something in the tank here as the climb ends with a quick ~13% kicker. For an extra challenge, continue the ride by turning left or right on the cobbled road.",
        "summary": "Sycamore is one of the prime Dirty Dozen hills, not because of its difficulty, but because of its use in the `Thrift Drug Classic`. Sycamore's actually one of the easier DD hills, but is also heavily trafficed by cars for much the same reason.",
        "related_segments": []
    },
